steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787823961
      nanos: 6119000
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_SYSTEM
    completed_at {
      seconds: 1787823961
      nanos: 6119000
    }
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Build a simple web frontend for a task-assignment system called WorkSphere, \nwith 3 user roles: admin, manager, employee. Use mock/in-memory data only \342\200\224 \nno real backend, database, or authentication provider.\n\nROLES & LOGIN\n- Simple login page: email + password fields.\n- Role is determined by the logged-in user\'s account, not selected by the user.\n- Seed exactly one hardcoded admin account: admin@test.com / password123\n- After successful login, redirect the user to their role\'s panel:\n  admin -> /admin, manager -> /manager, employee -> /employee\n- Block access to routes that don\'t match the logged-in user\'s role \n  (redirect back to login or show an access-denied message).\n\nDATA MODEL (mock/in-memory)\n- User: { id, name, email, password, role, team } \n  where role is exactly one of: \"admin\" | \"manager\" | \"employee\"\n  and team is a plain string (e.g. \"Engineering\", \"Design\").\n- Task: { id, title, status, assignedTo, team } \n  where assignedTo is a user id, team is a plain string matching a team name,\n  and status is one of: \"unassigned\" | \"pending review\" | \"resolved\"\n- Seed a few fake users across at least 2 different teams, and a few fake \n  tasks assigned to different mock employees, tagged with matching teams.\n\nADMIN PANEL (/admin)\n- A form to create a new user: name, email, password, role (dropdown: \n  manager or employee), team (text input or dropdown). New users are \n  added to the in-memory user list.\n- A table listing all existing users with columns: name, email, role, team.\n\nMANAGER PANEL (/manager)\n- A plain table of all tasks with columns: title, status, team. Use \n  seeded fake rows. No approve/reject actions needed yet.\n- A \"Sync now\" button above the table. On click, just show a temporary \n  message like \"Checking for new documents...\" followed by \"No new \n  documents found\" after ~1 second (simulate it \342\200\224 no real Drive \n  integration yet). Don\'t wire this to anything real.\n\nEMPLOYEE PANEL (/employee)\n- A plain table of tasks filtered to only the ones assigned to the \n  logged-in employee, columns: title, status, team. Use seeded fake rows.\n\nSTYLING\n- Keep it minimal and functional \342\200\224 plain layout, no theming, no branding. \n  Readability over polish. This is a first-pass skeleton, not a final UI.\n\nSCOPE\n- Do not add password reset, email verification, task creation forms, \n  search, filtering, approve/override logic, or any real Drive/API \n  integration \342\200\224 those come later. Keep this build limited exactly to \n  what\'s listed above. This is strictly a front-end shell for demonstration purposes.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Build a simple web frontend for a task-assignment system called WorkSphere, \nwith 3 user roles: admin, manager, employee. Use mock/in-memory data only \342\200\224 \nno real backend, database, or authentication provider.\n\nROLES & LOGIN\n- Simple login page: email + password fields.\n- Role is determined by the logged-in user\'s account, not selected by the user.\n- Seed exactly one hardcoded admin account: admin@test.com / password123\n- After successful login, redirect the user to their role\'s panel:\n  admin -> /admin, manager -> /manager, employee -> /employee\n- Block access to routes that don\'t match the logged-in user\'s role \n  (redirect back to login or show an access-denied message).\n\nDATA MODEL (mock/in-memory)\n- User: { id, name, email, password, role, team } \n  where role is exactly one of: \"admin\" | \"manager\" | \"employee\"\n  and team is a plain string (e.g. \"Engineering\", \"Design\").\n- Task: { id, title, status, assignedTo, team } \n  where assignedTo is a user id, team is a plain string matching a team name,\n  and status is one of: \"unassigned\" | \"pending review\" | \"resolved\"\n- Seed a few fake users across at least 2 different teams, and a few fake \n  tasks assigned to different mock employees, tagged with matching teams.\n\nADMIN PANEL (/admin)\n- A form to create a new user: name, email, password, role (dropdown: \n  manager or employee), team (text input or dropdown). New users are \n  added to the in-memory user list.\n- A table listing all existing users with columns: name, email, role, team.\n\nMANAGER PANEL (/manager)\n- A plain table of all tasks with columns: title, status, team. Use \n  seeded fake rows. No approve/reject actions needed yet.\n- A \"Sync now\" button above the table. On click, just show a temporary \n  message like \"Checking for new documents...\" followed by \"No new \n  documents found\" after ~1 second (simulate it \342\200\224 no real Drive \n  integration yet). Don\'t wire this to anything real.\n\nEMPLOYEE PANEL (/employee)\n- A plain table of tasks filtered to only the ones assigned to the \n  logged-in employee, columns: title, status, team. Use seeded fake rows.\n\nSTYLING\n- Keep it minimal and functional \342\200\224 plain layout, no theming, no branding. \n  Readability over polish. This is a first-pass skeleton, not a final UI.\n\nSCOPE\n- Do not add password reset, email verification, task creation forms, \n  search, filtering, approve/override logic, or any real Drive/API \n  integration \342\200\224 those come later. Keep this build limited exactly to \n  what\'s listed above. This is strictly a front-end shell for demonstration purposes.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
