    response: "I have built the frontend shell for **WorkSphere** according to your exact specifications:\n\n- **Authentication & Role Resolution**:\n  - Implemented a clean login form with email and password fields. Role is derived directly from the authenticated user\'s account with no manual role selection.\n  - Seeded the hardcoded administrator account (`admin@test.com` / `password123`), along with mock managers and employees across multiple teams (*Engineering* and *Design*).\n  - Integrated role-based routing and route guarding: users are directed to `/admin`, `/manager`, or `/employee` upon login, and unauthorized route access displays an access-denied view.\n\n- **Admin Panel (`/admin`)**:\n  - Form to create new users with name, email, password, role dropdown (*Manager* / *Employee*), and team input, updating the in-memory state.\n  - Structured table listing all registered users with name, email, role badge, and team.\n\n- **Manager Panel (`/manager`)**:\n  - Global overview table displaying all team tasks with title, status, and team tag.\n  - Interactive \"Sync now\" button simulating document discovery (\"Checking for new documents...\" followed by \"No new documents found\" after 1 second).\n\n- **Employee Panel (`/employee`)**:\n  - Dedicated task table filtered strictly to tasks assigned to the currently authenticated employee.\n\n- **Minimalist & Functional Layout**:\n  - High-readability, unbranded layout with clear typographic contrast and responsive tables."
    modified_response: "I have built the frontend shell for **WorkSphere** according to your exact specifications:\n\n- **Authentication & Role Resolution**:\n  - Implemented a clean login form with email and password fields. Role is derived directly from the authenticated user\'s account with no manual role selection.\n  - Seeded the hardcoded administrator account (`admin@test.com` / `password123`), along with mock managers and employees across multiple teams (*Engineering* and *Design*).\n  - Integrated role-based routing and route guarding: users are directed to `/admin`, `/manager`, or `/employee` upon login, and unauthorized route access displays an access-denied view.\n\n- **Admin Panel (`/admin`)**:\n  - Form to create new users with name, email, password, role dropdown (*Manager* / *Employee*), and team input, updating the in-memory state.\n  - Structured table listing all registered users with name, email, role badge, and team.\n\n- **Manager Panel (`/manager`)**:\n  - Global overview table displaying all team tasks with title, status, and team tag.\n  - Interactive \"Sync now\" button simulating document discovery (\"Checking for new documents...\" followed by \"No new documents found\" after 1 second).\n\n- **Employee Panel (`/employee`)**:\n  - Dedicated task table filtered strictly to tasks assigned to the currently authenticated employee.\n\n- **Minimalist & Functional Layout**:\n  - High-readability, unbranded layout with clear typographic contrast and responsive tables."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
